Verse 31. My harp also is turned to mourning] Instead of the harp, my only music is my own plaintive cries. 

  And my organ] What the bge uggab was, we know not; it was most probably some sort of pipe or wind instrument. His harp, rwnk kinnor, and his pipe, bge uggab, were equally mute, or only used for mournful ditties. 

THIS chapter is full of the most painful and pathetic sorrow; but nevertheless tempered with a calmness and humiliation of spirit, which did not appear in Job's lamentations previously to the time in which he had that remarkable revelation mentioned in the nineteenth chapter. {
